---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import Heading from '../components/typography/Heading.astro';
import Body from '../components/typography/Body.astro';
import DefinitionList from '../components/DefinitionList.astro';
import ReadingMetadata from '../components/ReadingMetadata.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { FileText, Triangle } from '@lucide/astro';

const expertiseItems = [
  {
    term: "Functional Programming",
    definition: "Separation of concerns through pure functions, immutable data, and composable architectures"
  },
  {
    term: "Distributed Systems",
    definition: "Building correct systems that handle millions of events while maintaining both velocity and correctness guarantees"
  },
  {
    term: "Real-Time Processing",
    definition: "Event-driven architectures with Kafka, exactly-once semantics, and graceful degradation"
  },
  {
    term: "Content Architecture",
    definition: "Editorial infrastructure for global→local fintech content, handling regulatory and cultural complexity"
  },
  {
    term: "Global Scaling",
    definition: "Fintech regulations, internationalization, and localization across diverse markets"
  },
  {
    term: "Platform Engineering",
    definition: "Infrastructure that lets teams deploy confidently through observability, testing, and progressive delivery"
  },
  {
    term: "Architecture Patterns",
    definition: "Domain-Driven Design, CQRS, event sourcing, and microservice decomposition"
  },
  {
    term: "LLM Integration",
    definition: "Cognitive partners revealing architectural possibilities, not automation replacing judgment"
  }
];
---

<Layout title="About - Saad Shahd">
  <Container width="narrow">
    <Heading level={1} as="h1" class="mb-16"><span>About</span></Heading>

    <div>
      <Body size="lg" as="p" class="text-text-lighter mb-8 leading-normal">
        What if we asked <i>why</i> before <i>how</i>? Over 15 years at Instabug, Statsbomb, and Wise, patterns emerged: when teams explore constraints first, architecture reveals itself through production needs.
      </Body>

      <Body size="base" as="p" class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
        At Wise, 20 teams across product, legal, and marketing edit the same pricing content—regulations collide with cultural nuances, offerings vary by market. The problem space is architectural: how do we maintain coherence and developer experience when constraints multiply? Building editorial infrastructure that handles global→local fintech tension through structural separation.
      </Body>

      <Body size="base" as="p" class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
        Functional programming principles emerged through production bugs at Instabug, Statsbomb, and Wise. Traditional thinking treats velocity and correctness as opposing forces. Working in high-velocity environments revealed they're complementary: when you separate behavior from state and make illegal states unrepresentable, both increase together. Still learning what's possible when architecture constrains failure.
      </Body>

      <Body size="base" as="p" class="mb-8 leading-relaxed">
        How do systems adapt when the future is unknowable? Over 15 years at Instabug, Statsbomb, and Wise, this pattern repeated: separating behavior from state, making illegal states unrepresentable, means systems can handle surprises structurally. Exploring how LLMs fit this pattern—not as automation replacing judgment, but as cognitive partners revealing architectural possibilities we haven't considered. Working primarily in TypeScript, Python, Go, and Clojure.
      </Body>

      <Callout variant="primary" size="compact">
        <div class="md:flex justify-between items-center">
          <div>
            <Triangle class="w-5 h-5 inline mr-1" />
            Curious about the <strong>why</strong> first—it sometimes reveals the <strong>how,</strong> but always clarifies what we're building.
          </div>
          <Button variant="primary" size="sm" href="#" class="mt-3 md:mt-0">Full Background</Button>
        </div>
      </Callout>

      

      <Heading level={1} as="h2" class="mt-12 mb-6"><span>Technical Expertise</span></Heading>
      <DefinitionList items={expertiseItems} />

    </div>
  </Container>
</Layout>
